1
00:00:48,950 --> 00:00:52,990
[The Old Story of Yu Hong]

2
00:00:53,260 --> 00:00:55,970
[Episode 20]

3
00:01:12,980 --> 00:01:19,350
[Limin Bookstore] [Cashier]

4
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:41,220
[HLA Test Report,
Tiedong District People's Hospital]

5
00:01:41,259 --> 00:01:42,930
[Chronicle of a Blood Merchant, by Yu Hua]

6
00:01:48,259 --> 00:01:50,500
This book leaves every reader upset.

7
00:01:51,509 --> 00:01:53,770
What's written seems
like everyday chatter,

8
00:01:53,770 --> 00:01:55,700
but deep down it hides bitterness.

9
00:01:55,890 --> 00:02:01,630
[Hao Jie, 29, patient]
[Liu Yang, 25, patient's boyfriend]

10
00:01:56,140 --> 00:01:57,940
Xu Sanguan isn't exactly smart.

11
00:01:58,570 --> 00:02:00,930
His first blood sale
is just to be part of the crowd.

12
00:02:00,930 --> 00:02:02,660
Then, he does it for his family,

13
00:02:02,710 --> 00:02:04,170
which is understandable.

14
00:02:05,010 --> 00:02:07,140
But what if it was for someone
outside the family?

15
00:02:07,140 --> 00:02:09,740
Everyone is a precious child
to their parents.

16
00:02:09,870 --> 00:02:10,960
If his parents knew

17
00:02:10,960 --> 00:02:12,420
their son risked his life,

18
00:02:13,420 --> 00:02:14,950
they would be heartbroken.

19
00:02:15,780 --> 00:02:16,840
Don't you think so?

20
00:02:52,040 --> 00:02:54,850
[Flowers bloom and wither,
clouds gather and scatter]

21
00:02:54,850 --> 00:03:02,680
[Six Records of a Floating Life]

22
00:03:26,410 --> 00:03:27,870
Why didn't you wait for me?

23
00:03:31,340 --> 00:03:32,970
I wanted to take a walk.

24
00:03:37,010 --> 00:03:38,000
Put this on.

25
00:03:50,680 --> 00:03:52,880
My recent test results are pretty good.

26
00:03:53,060 --> 00:03:55,250
You don't have to be out
with me every time.

27
00:03:55,250 --> 00:03:57,180
You just got a job and must be busy.

28
00:03:57,650 --> 00:03:59,850
Driving the company car out all the time

29
00:04:00,120 --> 00:04:02,520
will reflect badly on you,
if people see it.

30
00:04:05,120 --> 00:04:06,980
I know you hate riding in that car.

31
00:04:07,620 --> 00:04:09,750
Next time, I'll get a cab to pick you up.

32
00:04:11,360 --> 00:04:14,360
I plan to take a few days off
and spend some time at home.

33
00:04:14,360 --> 00:04:16,220
My mom keeps getting sick lately.

34
00:04:16,860 --> 00:04:18,519
Don't come meet me these days.

35
00:04:24,890 --> 00:04:25,820
Are you mad at me?

36
00:04:30,930 --> 00:04:31,390
Then...

37
00:04:32,630 --> 00:04:33,480
Then what do you mean?

38
00:04:33,480 --> 00:04:35,270
H-Have I said anything wrong?

39
00:04:42,420 --> 00:04:43,820
Did my sister talk to you?

40
00:04:44,770 --> 00:04:45,390
Did she?

41
00:04:47,950 --> 00:04:48,620
Please.

42
00:04:49,310 --> 00:04:50,480
I-If there's anything on your mind,

43
00:04:50,480 --> 00:04:51,870
just speak it out.

44
00:04:53,060 --> 00:04:54,800
Beat me or yell at me if you want.

45
00:04:54,800 --> 00:04:57,070
The way you're acting now
is making me nervous.

46
00:04:57,070 --> 00:04:58,870
What exactly do you mean by this?

47
00:05:01,250 --> 00:05:02,070
Liu Yang,

48
00:05:03,560 --> 00:05:04,500
let's break up.

49
00:05:04,750 --> 00:05:05,680
What did you say?

50
00:05:16,050 --> 00:05:16,930
I said...

51
00:05:21,270 --> 00:05:23,060
I want a breakup.

52
00:05:51,760 --> 00:05:52,880
The potatoes...

53
00:05:53,159 --> 00:05:54,690
You're cutting them into strips

54
00:05:54,690 --> 00:05:56,820
that can serve as load-bearing walls.

55
00:05:56,980 --> 00:05:58,240
How should I cut them then?

56
00:05:58,240 --> 00:06:00,250
Thick strips taste better.

57
00:06:00,250 --> 00:06:01,160
Super crispy.

58
00:06:01,160 --> 00:06:02,740
What's that nonsense now?

59
00:06:07,610 --> 00:06:09,340
You're back quite early today.

60
00:06:14,450 --> 00:06:15,980
Wash your hands for dinner.

61
00:06:17,730 --> 00:06:19,060
Want to wash your hands?

62
00:06:37,040 --> 00:06:37,970
Open your mouth.

63
00:06:39,010 --> 00:06:40,570
Why are you lying down?

64
00:06:40,890 --> 00:06:43,350
Did you eat something
at Wan Xiuhua's place?

65
00:06:43,680 --> 00:06:45,280
Your tummy's all puffed out.

66
00:06:45,500 --> 00:06:47,830
I have to eat your leftovers
at every meal.

67
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:20,890
I want chicken drumsticks.

68
00:07:22,720 --> 00:07:24,780
Slapping your thigh now, aren't you?

69
00:07:25,180 --> 00:07:26,980
Chicken butt also tastes great.

70
00:07:27,310 --> 00:07:30,310
So cunning. You won't let yourself
lose out even a bit.

71
00:07:40,890 --> 00:07:42,720
A grown man can get over whatever

72
00:07:44,100 --> 00:07:45,430
huge obstacles after a nice meal

73
00:07:45,430 --> 00:07:46,390
and a good sleep.

74
00:07:49,830 --> 00:07:51,770
I specially bought
this free-range chicken today.

75
00:07:51,770 --> 00:07:53,500
You're lucky to get to enjoy it.

76
00:07:54,720 --> 00:07:55,580
Have some more.

77
00:07:57,390 --> 00:07:57,950
Juan.

78
00:07:58,620 --> 00:08:00,220
I need to tell you something.

79
00:08:03,070 --> 00:08:04,270
I plan to get married.

80
00:08:10,390 --> 00:08:12,290
I'll soon bring my future wife home
for a proper meeting with you.

81
00:08:12,290 --> 00:08:14,020
Get me the household register.

82
00:08:16,800 --> 00:08:18,870
Don't put Sichuan pepper powder
on the fries next time.

83
00:08:18,870 --> 00:08:20,130
Nobody cooks this way.

84
00:08:26,830 --> 00:08:28,430
Have you thought it through?

85
00:08:36,480 --> 00:08:37,440
Let's have dinner first.

86
00:08:37,440 --> 00:08:39,440
Any discussion can wait till later.

87
00:09:04,460 --> 00:09:08,840
[Name: Hao Jie] [Household Register]

88
00:09:28,580 --> 00:09:29,630
What are you doing?

89
00:09:29,630 --> 00:09:31,030
It's no good if people see us like this.

90
00:09:31,030 --> 00:09:32,630
I don't care who might see us!

91
00:09:32,860 --> 00:09:34,990
Why did you suddenly ask for a breakup?

92
00:09:35,440 --> 00:09:37,200
I just had dumplings at your place
the day before yesterday.

93
00:09:37,200 --> 00:09:38,730
What on earth are you doing?

94
00:09:38,740 --> 00:09:40,140
Won't you go to Shanghai?

95
00:09:40,250 --> 00:09:41,500
Don't you want the money I owe you?

96
00:09:41,500 --> 00:09:42,250
What exactly are you up to?

97
00:09:42,250 --> 00:09:43,150
You must make it clear today!

98
00:09:43,150 --> 00:09:44,480
Or I won't let you leave.

99
00:09:44,700 --> 00:09:46,160
Stop being unreasonable.

100
00:09:46,250 --> 00:09:48,250
My sister talked to you, didn't she?

101
00:09:48,440 --> 00:09:49,770
Anyway, whatever reason there may be,

102
00:09:49,770 --> 00:09:51,370
I refuse to break up with you.

103
00:09:51,460 --> 00:09:53,370
I've loved you since high school.

104
00:09:53,370 --> 00:09:55,230
And I don't plan on changing that.

105
00:09:56,630 --> 00:09:58,200
I know you think you are a burden to me.

106
00:09:58,200 --> 00:09:59,740
But I don't care.

107
00:10:00,100 --> 00:10:01,250
I just want to see you every day.

108
00:10:01,250 --> 00:10:03,250
I'll do anything to keep you around.

109
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:07,060
Let's get married.

110
00:10:15,300 --> 00:10:17,140
All of these are yours now.

111
00:10:17,460 --> 00:10:18,580
I'll give you anything you want.

112
00:10:18,580 --> 00:10:19,750
I-In the future, I won't keep

113
00:10:19,750 --> 00:10:20,870
a single penny of what I earn.

114
00:10:20,870 --> 00:10:22,270
You can have my all, okay?

115
00:10:24,020 --> 00:10:25,660
Let's get a marriage certificate today.

116
00:10:25,660 --> 00:10:27,110
No, tomorrow.

117
00:10:27,140 --> 00:10:29,740
I don't have my household register
on me today.

118
00:10:30,300 --> 00:10:31,500
What's all this for?

119
00:10:31,500 --> 00:10:32,470
Listen up.

120
00:10:33,940 --> 00:10:35,540
I know this is not fair to you.

121
00:10:35,580 --> 00:10:37,700
I'm poor and I can't afford a ring.

122
00:10:37,700 --> 00:10:40,560
Our money has to be saved
for when we reach Shanghai.

123
00:10:40,820 --> 00:10:43,010
I'll make it up to you
when we get there, okay?

124
00:10:43,010 --> 00:10:44,620
Don't you like taking the train

125
00:10:44,620 --> 00:10:46,100
and hearing the station names?

126
00:10:46,100 --> 00:10:47,170
After you get a kidney transplant,

127
00:10:47,170 --> 00:10:49,300
I'll ride the train with you every day.

128
00:10:49,360 --> 00:10:50,770
We'll travel from south to north,

129
00:10:50,770 --> 00:10:52,050
and from east to west.

130
00:10:52,440 --> 00:10:54,300
I'll read the station names to you

131
00:10:54,370 --> 00:10:55,300
one by one, okay?

132
00:11:20,050 --> 00:11:21,360
Stop messing around.

133
00:11:24,700 --> 00:11:26,030
How am I messing around?

134
00:11:26,170 --> 00:11:28,410
I'm overjoyed
now that I'm getting married.

135
00:11:28,410 --> 00:11:30,370
I-I'm going to have a wife!

136
00:11:30,370 --> 00:11:31,810
I'm thrilled!

137
00:11:33,370 --> 00:11:34,890
I'm going to have a wife!

138
00:11:35,550 --> 00:11:37,390
I'm getting married!

139
00:11:41,200 --> 00:11:41,620
Come on!

140
00:11:41,620 --> 00:11:42,790
Cheers!

141
00:11:43,200 --> 00:11:43,860
Drink up.

142
00:11:46,510 --> 00:11:48,260
What? You had too much to drink?

143
00:11:48,940 --> 00:11:49,630
Go on, guys.

144
00:11:49,630 --> 00:11:51,090
I need to use the restroom.

145
00:11:51,510 --> 00:11:52,320
Where are you going?

146
00:11:52,320 --> 00:11:53,120
Let me check your pulse

147
00:11:53,120 --> 00:11:54,130
to see if you have kidney deficiency.

148
00:11:54,130 --> 00:11:55,120
What's the matter with you?

149
00:11:55,120 --> 00:11:55,960
Whenever it's time to pay,

150
00:11:55,960 --> 00:11:57,340
you always go to the restroom.

151
00:11:57,340 --> 00:11:58,750
I really need to take a dump.

152
00:11:58,750 --> 00:11:59,700
Cut it out!

153
00:11:59,700 --> 00:12:00,630
I paid last time.

154
00:12:00,630 --> 00:12:02,240
And the time before that, Si paid, right?

155
00:12:02,240 --> 00:12:02,940
I absolutely did.

156
00:12:02,940 --> 00:12:04,050
That cost me a fortune.

157
00:12:04,050 --> 00:12:05,750
It should be your turn this time, huh?

158
00:12:05,750 --> 00:12:06,100
Come on.

159
00:12:06,100 --> 00:12:07,510
Nature calls. Can't refute that, right?

160
00:12:07,510 --> 00:12:08,170
I just want to take a dump.

161
00:12:08,170 --> 00:12:09,840
Enough talking to him.
Get in his pockets. Search!

162
00:12:09,840 --> 00:12:10,840
Please don't.

163
00:12:10,840 --> 00:12:13,340
The stuffing's poking
out of my cotton pants.

164
00:12:13,340 --> 00:12:14,940
What? Keep searching, guys!

165
00:12:15,010 --> 00:12:16,480
My sister needs that for her treatment.

166
00:12:16,480 --> 00:12:17,700
You must be kidding me.

167
00:12:17,700 --> 00:12:18,460
What are you looking at?

168
00:12:18,460 --> 00:12:19,220
Hand it to me!

169
00:12:19,740 --> 00:12:20,370
Give me the bankbook.

170
00:12:20,370 --> 00:12:20,890
Keep searching!

171
00:12:20,890 --> 00:12:21,270
Hurry.

172
00:12:21,270 --> 00:12:22,080
There's over 30,000 yuan.

173
00:12:22,080 --> 00:12:22,510
Quick.

174
00:12:24,340 --> 00:12:25,200
Hand it over!

175
00:12:25,200 --> 00:12:25,740
My goodness.

176
00:12:25,740 --> 00:12:26,630
There is really over 30,000 yuan.

177
00:12:26,630 --> 00:12:28,670
What? Are you saving it
for when you get married, lad?

178
00:12:28,670 --> 00:12:29,840
Give it back to me now.

179
00:12:29,840 --> 00:12:30,550
It's for my sister's treatment.

180
00:12:30,550 --> 00:12:32,000
There really is over 30,000 yuan.

181
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:32,500
Give it back to me!

182
00:12:32,500 --> 00:12:33,860
-Hurry. Give it back to me!
-Sorry, guys.

183
00:12:33,860 --> 00:12:35,720
Well, I need to borrow
San Yan'er for a while.

184
00:12:35,720 --> 00:12:37,380
Look, you guys enjoy the meal.

185
00:12:38,360 --> 00:12:39,630
Enjoy yourselves.

186
00:12:39,630 --> 00:12:40,120
Sorry.

187
00:12:40,580 --> 00:12:41,820
You're not that big,
but you sure jump high.

188
00:12:41,820 --> 00:12:43,680
Messing with me all the time, huh?

189
00:12:50,870 --> 00:12:52,400
They easily cross the line.

190
00:12:54,870 --> 00:12:56,200
Does the Mercedes
before the Golden Imperial

191
00:12:56,200 --> 00:12:57,660
Dance Hall belong to Dong?

192
00:12:59,030 --> 00:13:01,630
Could you borrow it
and let me use it for one day?

193
00:13:02,580 --> 00:13:03,910
I won't do it for anyone,

194
00:13:04,820 --> 00:13:06,220
but you're an exception.

195
00:13:06,890 --> 00:13:08,200
Not only one car, even if

196
00:13:08,200 --> 00:13:09,000
you want ten,

197
00:13:09,700 --> 00:13:11,050
I'll have it done for you.

198
00:13:11,050 --> 00:13:11,910
Give it a break.

199
00:13:12,200 --> 00:13:13,130
What do you mean?

200
00:13:13,360 --> 00:13:14,690
You know me well or what?

201
00:13:17,370 --> 00:13:18,530
Don't you have a car?

202
00:13:19,630 --> 00:13:21,360
Why are you borrowing another?

203
00:13:23,200 --> 00:13:23,910
San Yan'er.

204
00:13:27,200 --> 00:13:29,400
You're going to have a brother-in-law.

205
00:13:34,720 --> 00:13:35,650
Who will that be?

206
00:13:44,520 --> 00:13:46,130
Ignorance really is bliss.

207
00:14:09,180 --> 00:14:10,670
It's right to say he grew up on handouts.

208
00:14:10,670 --> 00:14:11,710
Exactly.

209
00:14:13,620 --> 00:14:14,410
Sir.

210
00:14:16,130 --> 00:14:18,010
Five hundred skewers for this table.

211
00:14:18,010 --> 00:14:18,910
Got it!

212
00:14:19,250 --> 00:14:20,370
Are you trying to kill us with food?

213
00:14:20,370 --> 00:14:21,460
What's this about?

214
00:14:21,460 --> 00:14:22,000
What happened?

215
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:22,720
What's going on?

216
00:14:22,720 --> 00:14:25,240
Finally manning up for once
and going all out, aren't you?

217
00:14:25,240 --> 00:14:26,580
Get me ten cases of beer.

218
00:14:26,580 --> 00:14:28,200
Drink these fools to death.

219
00:14:28,200 --> 00:14:30,460
Sure thing, no problem. Coming right up.

220
00:14:32,520 --> 00:14:33,780
Wait, what's going on?

221
00:14:35,010 --> 00:14:36,080
Smartening up now, huh?

222
00:14:36,080 --> 00:14:37,370
I'm going to have a brother-in-law.

223
00:14:37,370 --> 00:14:39,700
What's the need to hold back?
Let's drink!

224
00:14:40,550 --> 00:14:41,200
Congratulations!

225
00:14:41,200 --> 00:14:42,750
-Guys.
-So much joy!

226
00:14:43,670 --> 00:14:44,250
Cheers!

227
00:15:04,290 --> 00:15:05,620
You've arrived, buddy.

228
00:15:06,120 --> 00:15:07,820
What took you so long? Traffic jams?

229
00:15:07,820 --> 00:15:08,870
Kind of.

230
00:15:09,700 --> 00:15:10,820
How have you been lately?

231
00:15:10,820 --> 00:15:11,750
Can't complain.

232
00:15:13,390 --> 00:15:14,650
Do you need to count it?

233
00:15:15,120 --> 00:15:16,270
What's the point of that?

234
00:15:16,270 --> 00:15:17,600
It's been so many years.

235
00:15:17,890 --> 00:15:20,090
When have Dong's goods ever gone wrong?

236
00:15:20,250 --> 00:15:21,310
So you do know that.

237
00:15:21,580 --> 00:15:22,010
Look.

238
00:15:22,700 --> 00:15:23,440
Take a seat somewhere.

239
00:15:23,440 --> 00:15:24,570
Let me check the pay.

240
00:15:24,940 --> 00:15:26,440
I'm busy. Make it quick.

241
00:15:29,630 --> 00:15:30,080
Hey, man,

242
00:15:30,080 --> 00:15:30,770
you're not a good friend.

243
00:15:30,770 --> 00:15:32,100
You never come visit me.

244
00:15:32,460 --> 00:15:34,480
And Dong gives my business little support.

245
00:15:34,480 --> 00:15:35,630
Dong is even busier.

246
00:15:37,870 --> 00:15:38,890
Why a new outfit?

247
00:15:39,890 --> 00:15:41,200
Nice belt.

248
00:15:43,360 --> 00:15:45,320
I heard your sister's getting married,
isn't she?

249
00:15:45,320 --> 00:15:46,380
You also know that?

250
00:15:47,120 --> 00:15:47,870
I'll invite you lot

251
00:15:47,870 --> 00:15:48,740
to the celebration.

252
00:15:48,740 --> 00:15:50,070
You definitely should.

253
00:15:50,320 --> 00:15:52,200
Better hold a proper wedding for her.

254
00:15:52,200 --> 00:15:54,940
You'll have to serve
the premium Chunghwa cigarettes then, huh?

255
00:15:54,940 --> 00:15:56,130
Even the mayor's daughter can't

256
00:15:56,130 --> 00:15:57,460
afford to serve those at her wedding.

257
00:15:57,460 --> 00:15:58,530
Aren't I just a small potato?

258
00:15:58,530 --> 00:15:59,740
Stop making fun of me.

259
00:15:59,740 --> 00:16:02,340
You're a big shot here in Tiecheng,
aren't you?

260
00:16:03,130 --> 00:16:04,130
What big shot?

261
00:16:05,200 --> 00:16:07,200
Dong's best, and I come second, huh?

262
00:16:10,620 --> 00:16:13,370
Why not serve
these fake Chunghwa cigarettes

263
00:16:13,370 --> 00:16:15,770
at your future brother-in-law's wedding?

264
00:16:24,740 --> 00:16:25,700
Are you trying to scare me?

265
00:16:25,700 --> 00:16:27,010
So what if I am?

266
00:16:30,080 --> 00:16:32,480
Could Dong possibly sell fake cigarettes?

267
00:16:45,630 --> 00:16:47,710
Hey, why did you flip over my car?
